# ASR pipeline

Whisper is not a native streaming model. Low latency = short overlapping windows + a resident CUDA model.

- Capture: WASAPI via PyAudio, 16 kHz mono, ~20 ms frames, lock-free ring buffer. **sounddevice** is the fallback if PyAudio cannot open a device.
- Windows: ~2.0 s audio, 250 ms hop for dictation. Meeting/Playback use ~6 s windows and an 800 ms hop so GPU load from video decode does not skip speech. `condition_on_previous_text=False`. `language=None`, `task="transcribe"`, `multilingual=True` so EN/FR/ZH (and mixed) stay in the spoken language. Stitch overlapping windows (CJK character tokens); commit only on `.` `?` `!` `。？！` (records also commit on a pause). Do not write sliding fragments twice.
- Model: `large-v3-turbo` (`turbo`), `device="cuda"`, `compute_type="float16"`. HUD Settings can pick another Faster-Whisper size (reload).
- `beam_size=1` on partials. Partials → overlay only. Whole-phrase voice commands (`paste last`, `copy last`, `correct last`) skip Ollama.
- Enable OFF must stop the stream, stop the VAD probe, and idle the ASR worker.
- Voice gate (RMS + spectral centroid) skips ASR on other speakers.
- VAD: after `vad_silence_ms` of quiet, stop the streaming mic and idle CUDA. A short blocking probe wakes capture on speech. Meeting Record keeps the stream open and mixes WASAPI speaker loopback with the microphone. Playback Record uses loopback only. Stitch overlapping windows; do not write sliding fragments to notes.
- Also gate on `no_speech_prob` and avg logprob. Do not overwrite clipboard on reject. No pyannote on the hot path.
